  "id": "u04-l04",
  "unit": "u04-food",
  "title": "I want…",
  "status": "draft",
  "tip": "**চাই** (*chai*) = 'I want'. It conjugates like খাই: তুমি **চাও**, আপনি **চান**. Careful not to confuse **চা** (tea) with **চাই** (want): **আমি চা চাই** = 'I want tea.'\n\nTo say you **want to do** something, put the verb in its **-তে** form first: খা- → **খেতে** (*khete*). **আমি ভাত খেতে চাই** = 'I want to eat rice.' (The vowel changes from আ to এ — just learn খেতে as a word.)\n\n**কিছু** = something/anything: **আপনি কিছু খেতে চান?** 'Would you like something to eat?'\n\nCulture: Bangladeshi hosts offer food again and again. A first **না, ধন্যবাদ** is often heard as politeness, so the offer will come back. If you really don't want more, say it warmly two or three times — or accept a little!\n\n**সমস্যা নেই** \"no problem\" and **অবশ্যই** \"of course\" are polite all-purpose replies. **আমার … দরকার** means \"I need …\".",
